  "description": "Dapper provider for DotNetBoost.MultiLingual. Translations live in one table, keyed by\n      (entity name, entity id, property name, language code), with the same schema the EF Core\n      provider maps — so a database can move between the two. Supports SQL Server, PostgreSQL and\n      SQLite, and can create its two tables at startup with UseDapper(..., migrateSchema: true).\n      There is no change tracker to hook, so application code localizes after a query and saves\n      translations alongside its own writes — see docs/dapper.md.",
